From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 22:02:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Assert on the shredded struct entries through the binding that is used

Unshred() in variant_unshredding.cpp takes the entries of the
shredded struct twice, once as child_vectors, which the function reads,
and once as child_entries, which only D_ASSERT() reads, so in a release
build, where D_ASSERT() expands to nothing, the second binding is
unused and -Wunused-variable says so. The assertion reads
child_vectors and the second binding goes, which is the shape upstream
gives the function later.

Carried here until the engine brings the same change.

---
 src/duckdb/src/storage/table/variant/variant_unshredding.cpp | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/storage/table/variant/variant_unshredding.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/storage/table/variant/variant_unshredding.cpp
index b0e90b2d28..10b82363d5 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/storage/table/variant/variant_unshredding.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/storage/table/variant/variant_unshredding.cpp
@@ -198,8 +198,7 @@ static vector<VariantValue> Unshred(UnifiedVariantVectorData &variant, Vector &s
 		// "typed_value", "untyped_value"
 		auto &child_vectors = StructVector::GetEntries(shredded);
 		D_ASSERT(shredded.GetType().id() == LogicalTypeId::STRUCT);
-		auto &child_entries = StructVector::GetEntries(shredded);
-		D_ASSERT(child_entries.size() <= 2);
+		D_ASSERT(child_vectors.size() <= 2);
 		typed_value_ref = *child_vectors[VariantColumnData::TYPED_VALUE_INDEX];
 		if (child_vectors.size() > 1) {
 			D_ASSERT(child_vectors.size() == 2);
